{"ds_fixture":{"provenance":"synthetic","seam":"vm/cow enumerate-writes virt-diff parse (D29; doc 01 sessions/01 spike)","created":"2026-06-14","note":"Hand-authored synthetic interleaved `virt-diff` capture that pins the DOCUMENTED single-line-CSV-record asymmetry between the per-row classifier (classifyRow/parseVirtDiffPerRow) and the whole-capture parseVirtDiffCSV. Row 1 is a plain `= /home/ds/.bashrc`; row 2 is a CSV-shaped `+,\"/home/ds/work/two<LF>line.md\"` whose RFC-4180 quoted path field carries an EMBEDDED LITERAL NEWLINE, splitting it across two physical lines. Because the capture is non-homogeneous (one plain row AND one CSV row), ModeAuto routes it to the per-row classifier, which bufio-scans line by line and feeds the FIRST physical line (`+,\"/home/ds/work/two`) to csv.Reader ALONE -> an unterminated-quote parse error: the physical newline is treated as a record boundary BEFORE csv.Reader can join the field. Whole-capture parseVirtDiffCSV, by contrast, reads the entire input with ONE csv.Reader and joins the field whole (`/home/ds/work/two\\nline.md`). Invented agent-workspace paths only; never a real session capture, never a real credential (D50). Guards the documented per-row limitation against silent regression."}}
